  "result": {
    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"The Tidyverse - Questionnaire\"\nengine: knitr\n---\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhat is the tidyverse in R? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_UEEILJKKGO'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UEEILJKKGO\" value=\"\"></input> <span>A function for generating random data</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UEEILJKKGO\" value=\"\"></input> <span>A package for interactive data visualization</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UEEILJKKGO\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>A collection of R packages for data manipulation and visualization</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_UEEILJKKGO\" value=\"\"></input> <span>A statistical model for data analysis</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich package in the tidyverse is used for data manipulation? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_KDNAZQOVCJ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KDNAZQOVCJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`ggplot2`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KDNAZQOVCJ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`dplyr`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KDNAZQOVCJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`tidyr`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KDNAZQOVCJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`readr`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich function in `dplyr` is used to filter rows based on certain conditions? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_CWDSQKMEVJ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CWDSQKMEVJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`group_by()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CWDSQKMEVJ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`filter()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CWDSQKMEVJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`mutate()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_CWDSQKMEVJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`arrange()`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nThe `pivot_longer()` function in `tidyr` is used to: <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_LUPVFJIUXJ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_LUPVFJIUXJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Merge two data frames based on a common column</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_LUPVFJIUXJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Reshape data from long to wide format</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_LUPVFJIUXJ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>Reshape data from wide to long format</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_LUPVFJIUXJ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Remove missing values from a data frame</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhat does the `mutate()` function in `dplyr` do? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_IXMVGZFBDO'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IXMVGZFBDO\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>Remove variables from a tibble</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IXMVGZFBDO\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>Add new variables or columns to a tibble</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IXMVGZFBDO\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Calculate summary statistics for a variable</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IXMVGZFBDO\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>Modify existing variables or create new ones based on transformations</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich function in `ggplot2` is used to add a title to a plot? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_GMIFGHGVXN'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_GMIFGHGVXN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`title()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_GMIFGHGVXN\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`ggtitle()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_GMIFGHGVXN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`add_title()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_GMIFGHGVXN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`main()`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nThe `select()` function in `dplyr` is used to: <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_FHTKUYQKRS'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FHTKUYQKRS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Group data by one or more variables</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FHTKUYQKRS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Arrange rows in ascending or descending order</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FHTKUYQKRS\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>Choose specific columns from a data frame</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FHTKUYQKRS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Filter rows based on a condition</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich package in the tidyverse is used for data import and export? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_ZMURHSCHRQ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZMURHSCHRQ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`readr`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZMURHSCHRQ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`ggplot2`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZMURHSCHRQ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`broom`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZMURHSCHRQ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`tidyr`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhat does the `arrange()` function in `dplyr` do? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_DZNWSNXSJF'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_DZNWSNXSJF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Calculate summary statistics for a variable</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_DZNWSNXSJF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Filter rows based on a condition</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_DZNWSNXSJF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>Group data by one or more variables</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_DZNWSNXSJF\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>Arrange rows in ascending or descending order</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich `forcats` function can be used to reorder factor levels based on a summary statistic? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_KJASQSQIFP'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KJASQSQIFP\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`fct_infreq()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KJASQSQIFP\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`fct_recode()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KJASQSQIFP\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`fct_reorder()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KJASQSQIFP\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`fct_relevel()`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich package from the tidyverse is dedicated to handling date and time data? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_ZLXOXVLPAY'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZLXOXVLPAY\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`lubridate`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZLXOXVLPAY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`tidyr`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZLXOXVLPAY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`forcats`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_ZLXOXVLPAY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`dplyr`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich function is used to group data by specific variables for aggregation? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_JNTCRCIRKW'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JNTCRCIRKW\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`group_by()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JNTCRCIRKW\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`summarise()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JNTCRCIRKW\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`gather()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JNTCRCIRKW\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`mutate()`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell class='webex-box'}\nWhich function is employed to create summary tables of data?] <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_MTNTGGJFMS'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_MTNTGGJFMS\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>`summarise()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_MTNTGGJFMS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`gather()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_MTNTGGJFMS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`arrange()`</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_MTNTGGJFMS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>`group_by()`</span></label></div>\n:::\n\n\n<br><br>\n\n::: {style=\"font-size: 0.875em;\"}\n[Back](/weeks/week-2.qmd) ⏎\n:::",
